# ET-8 generated task sets. The old rule excluded task_*.json as "regenerable: et8_env.py gen" --
# but NO SEED WAS EVER RECORDED, so v0 and v1 are not regenerable, and v0's files were never
# committed at all: its localisation numbers are permanently unauditable. The whole set is 7.8 MB
# and 0.2 MB gzipped, which was never the reason to exclude it. Ri's ruling after the v1 defect:
# every run persists the artifacts a later question could need, or its downstream claims are
# marked unauditable. So the task sets are TRACKED.
# experience/tasks/*/task_*.json
# experience/traj/  -- TRACKED, same ruling as the task sets. These are the trajectories every
# downstream claim reads: the A/C/F comparisons, the steering vectors, the probe, the G-trivial
# decomposition. et6's chess self-play games were kept only in memory and are GONE, which is why
# P8's adapter had nothing to confirm; v0's task files were never committed and its numbers are
# permanently unauditable. 26 MB total. Persist what a later question needs, or mark the claim.
!docs/series-completion-plan.md
!docs/et8b-loop-gates.md
!docs/whitepaper8.md
!docs/whitepaper8.html
!docs/whitepaper8.pdf
!docs/figs/
!docs/figs/*
!docs/efficient-thinking-1.md
!docs/efficient-thinking-1.html
!docs/efficient-thinking-1.pdf
!docs/efficient-thinking-2.md
!docs/efficient-thinking-2.html
!docs/efficient-thinking-2.pdf
!docs/efficient-thinking-3.md
!docs/efficient-thinking-3.pdf
!docs/efficient-thinking-8.md
!docs/efficient-thinking-8.html
!docs/efficient-thinking-8.pdf
!docs/et4-amendment-2-model-judge.md

# ET-8 spec and reading notes. docs/* ignores by default and every spec doc so far has been
# force-added one at a time, which means the NEXT one is silently untracked until someone notices.
# et8b-reading-note.md was: `git add` refused it and only the error revealed the rule.
# ET spec and reading notes. This list was written 09-20 as et2/3/4/6/8 and it was INCOMPLETE the
# next day: docs/et7-ee-prereg.md was refused because nothing covered et7. I patched the symptom
# (the patterns I happened to need) instead of the class. One pattern for every paper in the series:
!docs/et[0-9]*-*.md
!docs/et[0-9]*.md
!docs/series-execution-plan.md
!docs/efficient-thinking-10-concept.md
!docs/et10-review.md
!docs/et10-series-plan.md
!docs/efficient-thinking-11-concept.md
!docs/efficient-thinking-12-concept.md
!poetry/preferences/
!poetry/preferences/*
!docs/index.html
!docs/CNAME
!docs/efficient-thinking-3.html

# Third time a doc was silently refused (et7 09-22, wo312 09-22). Patterns per-prefix do not
# hold: the next doc always has a new prefix. Negate ALL markdown under docs/ and keep the
# binary/derived exclusions explicit below.
!docs/*.md
!docs/efficient-thinking-7.md
!docs/efficient-thinking-7.html
